{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GSCzUU1kSc2AsfatnXTBpA","type":"tool_result","content":"1049\t**Q10.** 🔵 Which of these is *not* listed among the factors kube-scheduler takes into account?\n1050\t\n1051\tA) How recently each candidate node was rebooted\n1052\tB) Individual and collective resource requirements\n1053\tC) Affinity and anti-affinity specifications\n1054\tD) Data locality\n1055\t\n1056\t**Q11.** 🔵 The kubelet is given a set of PodSpecs. What is its responsibility?\n1057\t\n1058\tA) To choose which node each PodSpec should run on\n1059\tB) To store the PodSpecs durably so that they survive a restart\n1060\tC) To ensure the containers described in those PodSpecs are running and healthy"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f9b02ac-049e-468e-9571-70af8edf8dd5","uuid":"b87805ed-1529-45b1-b57b-d46d151f3438","timestamp":"2026-08-24T19:44:03.190Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md","content":"**Q10.** 🔵 Which of these is *not* listed among the factors kube-scheduler takes into account?\n\nA) How recently each candidate node was rebooted\nB) Individual and collective resource requirements\nC) Affinity and anti-affinity specifications\nD) Data locality\n\n**Q11.** 🔵 The kubelet is given a set of PodSpecs. What is its responsibility?\n\nA) To choose which node each PodSpec should run on\nB) To store the PodSpecs durably so that they survive a restart\nC) To ensure the containers described in those PodSpecs are running and healthy","numLines":12,"startLine":1049,"totalLines":1322}}}
